See what the DSP answers when the topologies are registered

The upstream patch sends AVCS_CMD_REGISTER_TOPOLOGIES with apr_send_pkt() and
walks away without looking at the reply. If the DSP rejects it, the symptom
shows up much later and somewhere else: when committing the topology
(VSS_IVOCPROC_CMD_TOPOLOGY_COMMIT, 0x13198) with error 1, and when enabling
the vocproc (0x100c6) with error 8. Which is exactly what we have.

Two traces are added:

  - The DSP's reply to the registration, which nobody was looking at.
  - What is sent and whether the ADSP was ready when it was sent. The
    registration is done in q6core's probe, so the reasonable suspicion is
    that it arrives too early.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
@@ -104,6 +104,22 @@
 				core->fwk_version_supported = false;
 			core->resp_received = true;
 			break;
+		case AVCS_CMD_REGISTER_TOPOLOGIES:
+			/*
+			 * Nadie miraba esta respuesta: q6core_register_topologies
+			 * hace apr_send_pkt() y se va. Si el DSP rechaza el
+			 * registro, la topologia no queda disponible y el fallo
+			 * aparece mucho despues y muy lejos, al confirmarla
+			 * (VSS_IVOCPROC_CMD_TOPOLOGY_COMMIT falla con error 1).
+			 */
+			if (result->status)
+				dev_err(&adev->dev,
+					"el DSP rechaza registrar las topologias: %d\n",
+					result->status);
+			else
+				dev_info(&adev->dev, "topologias registradas\n");
+			core->resp_received = true;
+			break;
 		case AVCS_CMD_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE:
 			if (result->status == ADSP_EUNSUPPORTED)
 				core->get_state_supported = false;
@@ -461,6 +477,9 @@
 	}
 
 	size = *(const u32 *) (fw->data + topo_off);
+	dev_info(dev, "registrando topologias: %u bytes desde %s (adsp %s)\n",
+		 size, fw_name,
+		 q6core_is_adsp_ready() ? "listo" : "TODAVIA NO LISTO");
 	ret = q6core_register_topologies(dev, size, fw->data + topo_off + 4);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto release_fw;
